{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS9GcmsQjM9eCCjXxMAA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, here are the key findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController** (shipment/ShipmentController.kt:1-56): Currently has POST /shipments (create), GET /shipments/{id}, GET /shipments; uses ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException with ErrorCode enum\n2. **Shipment model** (shipment/Shipment.kt:9-13): Data class with status field using ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n3. **InMemoryShipmentRepository** (shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27): Provides save, findById, existsById methods\n4. **ErrorCode enum** (api/ApiError.kt:31-37): Defines error codes; currently has SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n5. **GlobalExceptionHandler** (api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28): Centralized exception-to-response mapping\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses with an ErrorCode and message string\n- GlobalExceptionHandler maps exceptions to JSON responses with error envelope: `{error: {code, message, fields}}`\n- Tests use MockMvc with status and jsonPath assertions, checking both status codes and error body structure (criterion #4 requires consistency)\n- All errors follow the ApiError envelope pattern\n\n**Affected files and why they cannot be avoided:**\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — must add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — must add tests for all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent CONFIRMED, CANCELLED rejection, missing shipment)\n3. **ApiError.kt** — must add a new ErrorCode for \"shipment in invalid state for confirmation\" (needed for the 409 CANCELLED case to be semantically correct with criterion #4)\n\n**Risks:**\n- The idempotent confirm case requires logic to detect already-CONFIRMED shipment and succeed silently rather than error\n- Adding ErrorCode to a shared file (api package) — but this is necessary infrastructure change, not unrelated refactoring\n\n**Open questions:** None that would change correct behavior. The ticket is clear on all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **api/ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum (line 36, before VALIDATION_FAILED). This code will be thrown when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **shipment/ShipmentController.kt** — Add new endpoint handler after the getById method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment { ... }\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Find shipment by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND if missing\n   - If status is CREATED, save with status=CONFIRMED and return it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return as-is (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n\n3. **shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status` — creates S-confirm-1, calls confirm, asserts 200 and status=CONFIRMED\n   - `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing` — creates S-confirm-2, confirms twice, both return 200 with status=CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — saves CANCELLED shipment to repo directly, confirms, asserts 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — calls confirm on non-existent ID, asserts 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered reusing the existing SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS error code for the CANCELLED case, but that violates criterion #4 (consistency) because the code would have a misleading semantic meaning. A new ErrorCode is necessary.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Check | Action | Write | Response |\n|------|------|-------|--------|-------|----------|\n| Create→Confirmed | findById(id) | status==CREATED | set status=CONFIRMED | save(updated) | 200 + Shipment |\n| Already Confirmed | findById(id) | status==CONFIRMED | no-op | (no write) | 200 + Shipment |\n| Cancelled | findById(id) | status==CANCELLED | throw | (no write) | 409 + ApiError(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) |\n| Not Found | findById(id) | null | throw | (no write) | 404 + ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) |\n\nAll error cases go through GlobalExceptionHandler which produces the ApiError envelope, maintaining criterion #4.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Normal transition (CREATED→CONFIRMED) exercises the main success path\n- Test 2: Idempotency (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED) ensures retry safety (criterion #5)\n- Test 3: Invalid state (CANCELLED rejection) exercises business logic constraint\n- Test 4: Missing resource exercises 404 path\n- All tests use MockMvc and check both status and error envelope structure\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by modifying the ApiError.kt file to add the new ErrorCode:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2488,"cache_read_input_tokens":20488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2488},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd3def2-a8f3-4113-9402-04a63f24d98e","uuid":"c012343f-4d27-4c20-8dc7-26453ee03938","timestamp":"2026-09-26T13:38:57.636Z","request_id":"req_011CfS9GcJbD8g9W6f3K8FrZ"}
